From 916f9a562b7b0931976daac15bc50789c5af2391 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pogo-bash <pogo-bash@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 01:27:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb: WebGL for embedders whose executor is WebGL itself

An in-process RemoteWebGLTransport (local_factory) for embedders without a compositor process, whose GL calls run
on a host WebGL context. Such an executor answers as the host does: getSupportedExtensions is the host's list (in
its order), getters (getParameter, tex/buffer/renderbuffer/vertex attrib/program/shader/sampler/query/indexed/
internalformat parameters, active infos, precision formats, uniforms) come from the host over glHostQueryCHITIN,
the unmasked strings are the host's, extension methods run on the host's extension (glHostExtensionCallCHITIN).
Adds WEBGL_lose_context, 36 extension interfaces named as Chrome names them, getSamplerParameter,
getTransformFeedbackVarying, getIndexedParameter, drawingBufferColorSpace and unpackColorSpace; host context loss
reaches the context (on_context_loss_change); deleted shaders and programs stay named while in use; unpack flip and
premultiply apply to array uploads on the executor; a negative bufferData size is INVALID_VALUE.
